Root cause:
The bug was caused by the inclusion of UNIX-specific constant initializations in the native code, which were not suitable for Windows builds. This led to compilation failures when attempting to compile the native code on non-UNIX platforms, particularly after changes made in HADOOP-7824 that affected platform compatibility.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
SET_INT_OR_RETURN(env, clazz, S_IXUSR);
```
Reason:
The inclusion of the UNIX-specific constant `S_IXUSR` in the code without any conditional compilation checks caused issues when compiling on Windows platforms. Since `S_IXUSR` is not defined for non-UNIX systems, this led to compilation failures after the changes introduced in HADOOP-7824 that broadened platform compatibility.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
+#ifdef UNIX
SET_INT_OR_RETURN(env, clazz, S_IXUSR);
+#endif
```
Reason:
The addition of the `#ifdef UNIX` preprocessor directive ensures that the line setting the UNIX-specific constant `S_IXUSR` is only compiled when the code is being built on a UNIX platform. This prevents the compilation failure on Windows by excluding this platform-specific code from being included in the build for non-UNIX systems.


